   "claim": "The 'Server settings reach the adapter' decision makes the bind address configurable on RestApp, but says nothing about ServerHandle.address(). The merged core hardcodes it to \"127.0.0.1\", and docs/api/app.md documents address() as `127.0.0.1`. With a LAN bind (D-212), the handle would report the wrong address unless the wave also changes it.",
   "evidence": "NaruServe-api/src/main/java/com/snoworca/naruserve/internal/DefaultRestApp.java:251,267; NaruServe-api/src/main/java/com/snoworca/naruserve/ServerHandle.java:10; docs/api/app.md:146; waves/wave-5/design.md:113",
   "suggested_fix": "Add to the settings decision: ServerHandle.address() reports the configured bind address (loopback by default), and update the ServerHandle javadoc and the docs/api/app.md line 146."
  }
 ]
